decisions:
  - id: quick-check-mode
    decision: Added mode='quick' to orchestrate_inline as lightweight pre-check
    rationale: Enforcement requires orchestration for 3+ files but full plan mode is heavy. Quick-check runs advocate + reviewer analysis in ~3-4k tokens, greenlights or escalates. Satisfies enforcement either way.
  - id: jinx-core-agent
    decision: Promoted Jinx (advocate) to 7th core agent across all project types
    rationale: Devil's advocate should run on every task, not just when manually added. Added to all 10 project type rosters, DEFAULT_MODELS (opus tier), ROLE_PROMPTS.
  - id: magnitude-scoring
    decision: Replaced file-count threshold with magnitude-based scoring in stop hook Check 13
    rationale: Raw file count missed cross-package and security-adjacent signals. Magnitude = files(1pt) + cross-pkg(2pt) + security-adjacent(2pt each) + symbol files(1pt).
  - id: habits-consolidation
    decision: Made MCP habits-loader the single source of truth, CLI re-exports
    rationale: Two evaluators with divergent check types caused bugs (v5.21.3). Added 4 missing check types to MCP, CLI evaluator.ts became a thin re-export.
  - id: readme-rewrite-approach
    decision: README rewrite on side branch with AI-first prompt patterns
    rationale: 'Team analysis (DX, Product, Jinx) agreed: lead with paradigm shift, make agent team front and center, show natural language prompts alongside CLI commands. Branch for preview before merging.'
learnings:
  - 'Quick-check mode should auto-escalate conservatively: 2+ signals or any security/critical signal triggers full orchestration'
  - 'The README''s actual audience is one person: a developer deciding whether to try Paradigm in the next 5 minutes'
  - 'AI-first documentation pattern: show the prompt you''d say to your AI, then show what runs underneath — users talk to their AI, not their terminal'
  - 'Neverland pillars analysis: all 4 teams agreed A/B framework must be 3 variants (bare model vs hand-written prompt vs PAN agent) — only C>B validates the product'
